# LOCKS: who is editing a SHARED file right now. One line per lock:
#   <path>  <agent>  <task>  <UTC time>
# A file only one task touches (its own hero's data/docs/plugins/tests) needs no lock.
# Protocol (the push to /upstream is atomic, so a lock is taken only if the push wins):
#   take:    git pull --rebase; check the path is not listed; append your line; commit "lock: <path> <agent>"; git push.
#            Push rejected -> git pull --rebase; if the path is now someone else's, wait and retry; else push again.
#   release: in the SAME push as your finished work, delete your line (commit "unlock: <path> <agent>").
#   Never edit a path locked by another agent. Never remove another agent's line.
